close_reason: MCP host journey verified against the published 2026.10.15 artifact over stdio and Streamable HTTP
body: "## End-to-end journey\n\n- Discover supported protocol versions, server identity, core capabilities, and extensions.\n- Send any request with explicit request-local version and client capability metadata.\n- List and call deterministic token-bounded pm tools, prompts, and resources.\n- Respond to input_required results and retry the original request with inputResponses.\n- Observe request progress and opted-in list or resource changes without connection-local state.\n- Run long operations through durable task handles and application-level pm cursors.\n- Receive actionable structured refusals for unsupported versions, missing capabilities, invalid schemas, authorization failures, and expired handles.\n- Verify the same journey against a packed and published installation."
